---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { profile, href } from '../config';
---

<Base title="About & contact">
  <section class="page-intro wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE PROJECTS</p>
    <h1>
      Hi, I’m Sunny Sharma.
      <br />
      <em>Always building.</em>
    </h1>
    <p>{profile.description}</p>
  </section>
  <section class="about-grid wrap section">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>A foundation in real systems</h2>
      <p>
        At Everlytics Data Science, I progressed from Data Engineering Intern to
        Data Engineer and Senior Data Engineer. My work covered enterprise
        warehouse migrations, ETL delivery, orchestration, validation, and
        production support across engineering, analytics, and business teams.
      </p>
      <p>
        I contributed to a Teradata-to-SingleStore migration spanning more than
        100 TB and migrated or optimized over 100 Informatica workflows. I later
        led orchestration and delivery activities for migration of more than 10
        business-critical modules and 10 TB of historical data to a lakehouse
        architecture.
      </p>
      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <h3>Senior Data Engineer · Everlytics</h3>
      <p>November 2025 – May 2026 · Bengaluru</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Coordinated Airflow workflows for batch, CDC, and streaming ingestion,
          including scheduling, dependencies, validation, and operational
          execution.
        </li>
        <li>
          Supported modernization of Java, Node.js, and shell processing logic
          into Python workflows.
        </li>
        <li>
          Owned troubleshooting and performance-tuning activities, and
          coordinated testing, release stabilization, and handover.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Data Engineer · Everlytics</h3>
      <p>February 2023 – November 2025 · Bengaluru</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Developed, migrated, and optimized Informatica ETL and SQL
          transformations for the Teradata-to-SingleStore migration.
        </li>
        <li>
          Redesigned more than 30 workflows and supported source-to-target
          validation, failed-load diagnosis, monitoring, and deployment.
        </li>
        <li>
          Mentored five junior engineers on ETL standards, validation, reviews,
          and production troubleshooting.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Data Engineering Intern · Everlytics</h3>
      <p>July 2022 – January 2023</p>
      <p>
        Evaluated SingleStore and MariaDB ColumnStore as Teradata alternatives
        through replication, ETL migration, and benchmarking with datasets of
        more than 40 million records.
      </p>
      <h2>A pipeline I owned end to end</h2>
      <p>
        I built, tested, deployed, and supported an Informatica-scheduled
        flat-file pipeline into SingleStore. Compressed files of approximately
        5–10 MB arrived every five minutes, with a processing SLA below five
        minutes. A shell script unzipped and validated each file before a
        truncate-and-load landing step. Staging transformations cleaned and
        prepared the data for dimension and fact loading.
      </p>
      <p>
        The workflow maintained SCD Type 2 history across approximately three to
        five dimensions. Joins and unique-key combinations identified changed
        fact records; unchanged records were skipped. Rejected landing/staging
        records went to Informatica bad-record files, and conditional shell
        tasks sent success or failure emails. Final tasks archived source files
        and cleaned the processing directory. Informatica parallel processing
        supported ingestion performance.
      </p>
      <p>
        This pipeline did not include reconciliation. That is a concrete area I
        would improve with source/target control totals and completeness checks.
        In a separate project, I used OpenMetadata for scheduled data-quality
        checks.
      </p>
      <h2>Independent GenAI development</h2>
      <p>
        Since June 2026, I have focused on independent applications for document
        question answering, tool-using agents, and natural-language SQL. My work
        combines Python, FastAPI, LangChain, LangGraph, vector retrieval,
        Docker, testing, and trace-based debugging. The{' '}
        <a href={href('projects/')}>project case studies</a> explain the
        implementation, evidence, and remaining work.
      </p>
      <h2>How I approach the work</h2>
      <p>
        Start with a specific problem. Keep system boundaries clear. Test what
        can be tested deterministically, and separate that evidence from model
        behavior. Document the limitations alongside the implementation.
      </p>
      <p>
        The GenAI work here represents independent portfolio development, rather
        than commercial production GenAI experience.
      </p>
      <h2>Education</h2>
      <p>M.Tech. in Biotechnology · UIET, Kurukshetra University · 2019–2021</p>
      <p>
        B.Tech. in Biotechnology · Maharshi Dayanand University, Rohtak ·
        2014–2018
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="about-aside">
      <p class="eyebrow">MY TOOLBOX</p>
      <h3>Production foundations</h3>
      <p>
        Python · SQL · Airflow · Informatica
        <br />
        SingleStore · Teradata · PostgreSQL · ETL · Validation · Monitoring
      </p>
      <h3>Applied AI projects</h3>
      <p>
        LangChain · LangGraph · RAG · Tool calling
        <br />
        FastAPI · FAISS · pgvector · Docker · Pytest · GitHub Actions
      </p>
      <h3>Roles I’m pursuing</h3>
      <p>Python + GenAI Engineer · Applied AI Engineer · AI Data Engineer</p>
      <p>
        Full-time roles in Delhi NCR, including Noida and Gurugram. Open to
        remote short-term project collaboration.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </section>
  <section class="contact-band wrap" id="contact">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">LET’S CONNECT</p>
      <h2>
        Talk projects.
        <br />
        Explore possibilities.
      </h2>
      <p>
        Email me for my latest resume, a project walkthrough, or a conversation
        about your team’s engineering needs.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="contact-links">
      <a class="button" href={profile.github}>
        Find me on GitHub ↗
      </a>
      {profile.email && <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>}
      {profile.linkedin && <a href={profile.linkedin}>LinkedIn ↗</a>}
      {profile.resume && (
        <a href={href(profile.resume)} download>
          Download résumé ↓
        </a>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
